To create new repo:
--> First create it on the website
Then go to the terminal and  in your repository you want to commit

1. Create a .gitignore
Ex. https://gist.github.com/octocat/9257657
BE SURE TO ADD *.png and *.root files to it as well!

git init                 → make local directory a Git repo
git add .                → stage files
git commit -m "first commit"               → create local commit
git branch -M main                         → name branch "main"
git remote add origin git@github.com:mehmoo24/ComputeFluxConstraint.git    → connect local repo to GitHub
git pull --rebase origin main          → CAN SKIP if nothing there otherwise: bring down existing GitHub commits
git push -u origin main                → upload your local commits


